  "body": "## Research consolidation \u2014 no new kappa\n\nResolves the explicit batch970 request to reconcile **PR279's complete 116-file parent inventory** with its original reviewed source and incorporated #828 companion. Source head: `913ccc48a0bc1173709ea92280b96252256b7754`; research base: `1b59b624d21924f8e3537cdc1ac52d3be6eda2fe`; OS-random assignment seed **97**.\n\n### New evidence, not a duplicate replay\n\n#828 (mihir-s-05) already reconstructed the later package and ran its nine-stage finite verifier. This PR reuses that work explicitly; it does **not** claim a new mathematical replay. It adds:\n\n- an offline proof authenticating the raw reviewed/current Git commits and **27 Git trees**, binding every source byte and file mode to the fixed commit IDs;\n- an exact check of all **104 retained + 12 companion = 116 parent paths**, including every previously matched path/blob rather than only that list's size;\n- a **repository-wide**, commit-to-commit Merkle-tree difference: exactly **10 modified + 2 added files**, precisely the existing companion update, with no additional change hidden outside the assumed package;\n- one positive case and **17 corruption/omission/substitution controls**;\n- an updated ledger priority linking the resolved source-coverage question while preserving the parent's disposition and all original frozen sources.\n\nBoth original commits, source archives, selected frontier and predecessor receipts remain unchanged. PR279's acceptance/closure remains a maintainer decision; this PR does not close it.\n\n### Reproduce and observed verification\n\n```sh\npython3 -B research/pr279-parent-closure/verify.py\npython3 -I -O -B research/pr279-parent-closure/test_verify.py\n```\n\nObserved on Python **3.14.4**: `PASS_PR279_PARENT_COMMIT_CLOSURE`; `parent_paths=116`, `retained_paths=104`, `companion_paths=12`, `authenticated_commits=2`, `authenticated_trees=27`; all **18 tests passed** (`Ran 18 tests in 17.764s`, `OK`). No Git executable, network, `.git` directory, SymPy, or expensive mathematical replay is needed by these checks. A separate deterministic collector is included to recapture the frozen proof from original Git objects.\n\nExact report, source pins, limits, three compared candidates and final overlap refresh are under `research/pr279-parent-closure/`. The nine reused mathematical stages remain explicitly marked `fresh_execution=false`. No new selected-frontier cold replay, Lean build or hosted CI execution is claimed. Git SHA-1 source identity is a trust assumption, not an authorship/signature proof. All inherited compiler/geometry/restoration/routing/precision/analytic assumptions remain.\n\n### Credit and coordination\n\nAdam Gall (@adamgall), with substantial **OpenAI Codex assistance**. Predecessors: **mihir-s-05 (#828)** for reconstruction/replay; **Rohan Arun (#279)**, **eumemic (#268)**, **DreamingOfClouds (#276)**, **Douglas Colkitt** and the retained full source lineage. Original Apache-2.0 licenses and assistance disclosures remain intact.\n\nClaim: https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/1166#discussioncomment-18908144\n\nDistinct from PR116 evidence-only reconciliation (#1007), selected PR1042 capsule closure (#1142), and PR225 pricing consolidation (#1110).\n",
